N (1-based lines, blank lines skipped, an unterminated last line checked) and exits 1 if any, 0 if none\".\nRun: create clean.jsonl = `{\"a\":1}\\n{\"b\":2}\\n`; bad.jsonl = `{\"a\":1}\\n\\n{oops\\n{\"c\":3}\\n` (bad row is line 3, line 2 blank); torn.jsonl = `{\"a\":1}\\n{\"b\":` (no trailing newline, bad row line 2); multi.jsonl = `nope\\n{\"a\":1}\\n   \\n[1,\\n` (bad rows lines 1 and 4). For each run `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <path>; echo $?`.\nPASS: clean.jsonl prints no error lines and exits 0; bad.jsonl prints exactly one line starting with `<path>:3: ` followed by a non-empty error and exits 1; torn.jsonl prints a line starting with `<path>:2: ` and exits 1; multi.jsonl prints one line each for lines 1 and 4 (and none for the blank/whitespace line 3) and exits 1. FAIL: any missing or extra error line, wrong line number, blank line reported, torn last line not reported, line not in the `<file>:<line>: <error>` shape, or wrong exit code.\n\nCheck 2 — expect: \"A missing file or no argument prints to stderr and exits 2\".\nRun: `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js /nonexistent/x.jsonl; echo $?` and `node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js; echo $?`, capturing stderr separately.\nPASS: both exit 2 and both write something to stderr. FAIL: either exits with another status or writes nothing to stderr.\n\nCheck 3 — expect: \"packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js exports lint(text) returning [{ line, error }]\".\nRun: `node --input-type=module -e \"import {lint} from './packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js'; console.log(JSON.stringify(lint('{\\\"a\\\":1}\\n{bad\\n')), JSON.stringify(lint('{\\\"a\\\":1}\\n')))\"`.\nPASS: lint is an exported function; the first result is an array containing an object with line 2 and an error value; the second is an empty array. FAIL: no export named lint, not an array, or entries lack line/error.\n\nCheck 4 — expect: \"The workspace has its own package.json (jsonl-lint, type module, test script node --test), no runt